<div class="split"><article class="reading" lang="en" dir="ltr"><div class="row wrap"><x-prototype.badge tone="info">Grammar</x-prototype.badge><span class="muted"><x-prototype.icon name="clock"/> 15 minute lesson</span><x-prototype.badge>Free</x-prototype.badge></div>@include('prototype.partials.lesson-arabic')<h2>Let the action take the spotlight.</h2><p>We use the passive voice when the action, or the person receiving the action, is more important than who does it.</p><div class="example-block"><span class="eyebrow">Compare these sentences</span><p><strong>Active:</strong> Students organize the event.</p><p><strong>Passive:</strong> The event is organized by students.</p></div><h2>How do we form it?</h2><p>Use the verb <strong>be</strong> in the correct tense, followed by the <strong>past participle</strong> of the main verb.</p><div class="formula" dir="ltr">Subject + be + past participle</div><div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Passive voice examples" tabindex="0"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Tense</th><th scope="col">Active</th><th scope="col">Passive</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Present simple</td><td>They clean the room.</td><td>The room is cleaned.</td></tr><tr><td>Past simple</td><td>They cleaned the room.</td><td>The room was cleaned.</td></tr><tr><td>Future simple</td><td>They will clean the room.</td><td>The room will be cleaned.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2>When do we use “by”?</h2><p>Add <strong>by</strong> when the person doing the action is useful information. If the person is unknown or unimportant, you can leave it out.</p><blockquote>English is spoken in many countries.</blockquote><p>Here, the action matters more than the individual speakers.</p>@include('prototype.partials.lesson-media')<div class="actions"><button class="button button-primary" data-simulate="Lesson completion preview. Your progress has not been saved."><x-prototype.icon name="check"/> Mark as complete</button><x-prototype.link to="G12">Practise this lesson <x-prototype.icon name="arrow"/></x-prototype.link></div><p class="notice success" data-feedback role="status" hidden></p></article><aside class="stack"><x-prototype.card><h3>In this lesson</h3><p>1. Understand the passive voice</p><p>2. Form passive sentences</p><p>3. Use “by” naturally</p><x-prototype.progress :value="60" label="Sample lesson progress"/></x-prototype.card><x-prototype.card><h3>Before you begin</h3><p>It helps to know past participles and the verb “be”.</p><x-prototype.link to="S03">Review preparation</x-prototype.link></x-prototype.card><x-prototype.card><h3>Learn your way</h3><a href="{{ $url('G20') }}">Watch the video explanation →</a><a href="{{ $url('G18') }}">Open the study guide →</a><a href="{{ $url('G15') }}">Try the unit exam →</a><a href="{{ $url('G10') }}">Explore the topic →</a></x-prototype.card><x-prototype.card class="soft-card"><x-prototype.icon name="message"/><h3>Something not clicking?</h3><p>Ask a question with this lesson attached.</p><a class="button button-secondary" href="{{ $url('S14') }}?context=passive-voice">Ask your teacher</a></x-prototype.card>@if($emptyRecommendations)
